cells:
  - kind: 1
    value: "# Airline Reservation System\nOracle database, schema `ARS`. Run a cell with **Ctrl+Alt+Enter**. Every cell undoes its own changes, so any cell can be run again."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Ready check\nShould say **READY**. If not, reset the data from a terminal:\n\n`docker compose exec oracle bash /container-entrypoint-startdb.d/10_rebuild_ars.sh`"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Is the sample data fresh, and exactly as we loaded it?\nSELECT CASE\n         WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bookings) <> 18\n           THEN 'CHANGED - a run left changes behind. Reset the data.'\n         WHEN departure_time > SYSDATE + 2/24 AND departure_time < SYSDATE + 1\n           THEN 'READY'\n         ELSE 'STALE - flight dates have moved on. Reset the data.'\n       END                                             AS status,\n       ROUND((departure_time - SYSDATE) * 24, 1)       AS hours_until_flight_13_leaves,\n       (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bookings)                 AS bookings_now\n  FROM flights\n WHERE flight_id = 13;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Database map\n11 tables. A bar means one, a crow's foot means many.\n\n![Database map](airline_erd_overview.png)"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Book a ticket\nOne call books the seat and takes the payment. Triggers mark the seat and write the audit log."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET AUTOCOMMIT OFF\nSET SERVEROUTPUT ON\n-- Nikhil (passenger 16) books seat 1B, business class, on flight 2, and pays by UPI.\nDECLARE\n  v_booking bookings.booking_id%TYPE;\nBEGIN\n  book_ticket(p_passenger_id => 16,\n              p_flight_id    => 2,\n              p_seat_no      => '1B',\n              p_method       => 'UPI',\n              p_booking_id   => v_booking);\n  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Booking created: number ' || v_booking);\nEND;\n/\n-- 1) The ticket, as Nikhil sees it:\nSELECT booking_id, passenger_name, flight_no, seat_no, seat_class,\n       booking_status, amount_paid, payment_status\n  FROM passenger_itinerary\n WHERE booking_id = (SELECT MAX(booking_id) FROM bookings);\n-- 2) The seat is now taken, so one seat fewer is left:\nSELECT seat_no, status AS seat_status, seats_left(2) AS seats_left\n  FROM seats\n WHERE flight_id = 2 AND seat_no = '1B';\n-- 3) The diary line the database wrote all by itself:\nSELECT log_id, booking_id, action, old_status, new_status\n  FROM booking_audit_log\n WHERE booking_id = (SELECT MAX(booking_id) FROM bookings)\n ORDER BY log_id;\nROLLBACK;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Double booking is blocked\nThe same seat, through `book_ticket` and by a direct `INSERT`."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET AUTOCOMMIT OFF\nSET SERVEROUTPUT ON\nDECLARE\n  v_booking bookings.booking_id%TYPE;\n  v_other   bookings.booking_id%TYPE;\nBEGIN\n  -- Nikhil books seat 1B\n  book_ticket(16, 2, '1B', 'UPI', v_booking);\n\n  -- Front door: passenger 17 asks for the same seat the normal way\n  BEGIN\n    book_ticket(17, 2, '1B', 'CARD', v_other);\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - the front door should have been stopped');\n  EXCEPTION\n    WHEN OTHERS THEN\n      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Front door: The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\n  END;\n\n  -- Back door: passenger 17 types the booking in directly\n  BEGIN\n    INSERT INTO bookings (passenger_id, seat_id, status)\n    VALUES (17, (SELECT seat_id FROM seats WHERE flight_id = 2 AND seat_no = '1B'), 'CONFIRMED');\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - the back door should have been stopped');\n  EXCEPTION\n    WHEN OTHERS THEN\n      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Back door : The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\n  END;\nEND;\n/\nROLLBACK;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## One seat per person per flight\nA second seat on the same flight is refused (compound trigger)."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET AUTOCOMMIT OFF\nSET SERVEROUTPUT ON\nDECLARE\n  v_booking bookings.booking_id%TYPE;\n  v_second  bookings.booking_id%TYPE;\nBEGIN\n  -- Nikhil (passenger 16) books seat 1B\n  book_ticket(16, 2, '1B', 'UPI', v_booking);\n  -- ...and now asks for a second seat, 10D, on the same flight\n  BEGIN\n    book_ticket(16, 2, '10D', 'CARD', v_second);\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - a second seat should have been stopped');\n  EXCEPTION\n    WHEN OTHERS THEN\n      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\n  END;\nEND;\n/\nROLLBACK;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Failed payment is rolled back\nThe booking is undone too. The counts are the same before and after."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET AUTOCOMMIT OFF\nSET SERVEROUTPUT ON\n-- BEFORE: how many bookings and payments, and is seat 10D free?\nSELECT (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bookings) AS total_bookings,\n       (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM payments) AS total_payments,\n       (SELECT status FROM seats WHERE flight_id = 2 AND seat_no = '10D') AS seat_10d\n  FROM dual;\n\n-- Try 1: the passenger pays INR 100 for a 4,200 seat. The booking is written first,\n-- then the payment is declined, and the database undoes the booking.\nDECLARE\n  v_booking bookings.booking_id%TYPE;\nBEGIN\n  book_ticket(p_passenger_id => 17, p_flight_id => 2, p_seat_no => '10D',\n              p_method => 'CARD', p_booking_id => v_booking, p_amount_paid => 100);\n  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - the payment should have been declined');\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Payment too small: The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\nEND;\n/\n\n-- Try 2: the passenger pays with a made-up method (\"BITCOIN\"). Also undone.\nDECLARE\n  v_booking bookings.booking_id%TYPE;\nBEGIN\n  book_ticket(p_passenger_id => 17, p_flight_id => 2, p_seat_no => '10D',\n              p_method => 'BITCOIN', p_booking_id => v_booking);\n  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - BITCOIN should have been refused');\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Made-up payment method: The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\nEND;\n/\n\n-- AFTER: nothing changed. No half-made booking, no payment, the seat is still free.\nSELECT (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bookings) AS total_bookings,\n       (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM payments) AS total_payments,\n       (SELECT status FROM seats WHERE flight_id = 2 AND seat_no = '10D') AS seat_10d\n  FROM dual;\nROLLBACK;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Cancel and refund\n90 percent back, the seat is freed, the audit log is updated."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET AUTOCOMMIT OFF\nSET SERVEROUTPUT ON\n-- Nikhil books seat 1B and then cancels it. Flight 2 leaves in about 5 days.\nDECLARE\n  v_booking bookings.booking_id%TYPE;\n  v_refund  payments.refund_amount%TYPE;\nBEGIN\n  book_ticket(16, 2, '1B', 'UPI', v_booking);\n  cancel_booking(v_booking, v_refund);\n  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Money handed back to Nikhil: INR ' || v_refund);\nEND;\n/\n-- The ticket is now CANCELLED and the payment is REFUNDED:\nSELECT booking_id, passenger_name, seat_no, booking_status, amount_paid,\n       refund_amount, payment_status\n  FROM passenger_itinerary\n WHERE booking_id = (SELECT MAX(booking_id) FROM bookings);\n-- The seat is free again:\nSELECT seat_no, status AS seat_status, seats_left(2) AS seats_left\n  FROM seats\n WHERE flight_id = 2 AND seat_no = '1B';\n-- The diary shows the booking, then the cancellation:\nSELECT log_id, booking_id, action, old_status, new_status\n  FROM booking_audit_log\n WHERE booking_id = (SELECT MAX(booking_id) FROM bookings)\n ORDER BY log_id;\nROLLBACK;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Refund tiers\n90 percent at 3 or more days before departure, 50 percent at 1 to 3 days, 10 percent under a day, nothing after departure."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET AUTOCOMMIT OFF\nSET SERVEROUTPUT ON\nDECLARE\n  v_booking bookings.booking_id%TYPE;\n  v_refund  payments.refund_amount%TYPE;\nBEGIN\n  -- Flight 10 leaves in about 2 days: book a seat and cancel it (50 percent back)\n  book_ticket(16, 10, '10A', 'CARD', v_booking);\n  cancel_booking(v_booking, v_refund);\n  -- Flight 13 leaves within a day: cancel the seat that is already booked (10 percent back)\n  BEGIN\n    cancel_booking(13, v_refund);\n  EXCEPTION\n    WHEN OTHERS THEN\n      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Could not cancel booking 13 -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1) || '  (if that flight has left, reset the data)');\n  END;\nEND;\n/\nROLLBACK;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Refused cancellations\nCancelled twice, flight already departed, booking does not exist."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET AUTOCOMMIT OFF\nSET SERVEROUTPUT ON\nDECLARE\n  v_booking bookings.booking_id%TYPE;\n  v_refund  payments.refund_amount%TYPE;\nBEGIN\n  -- Cancelling the same booking twice\n  book_ticket(16, 2, '1B', 'UPI', v_booking);\n  cancel_booking(v_booking, v_refund);\n  BEGIN\n    cancel_booking(v_booking, v_refund);\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - cancelling twice should have been stopped');\n  EXCEPTION\n    WHEN OTHERS THEN\n      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Cancel twice          : The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\n  END;\n  -- A flight that has already left (booking 14)\n  BEGIN\n    cancel_booking(14, v_refund);\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - a departed flight should have been stopped');\n  EXCEPTION\n    WHEN OTHERS THEN\n      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Flight already left   : The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\n  END;\n  -- A ticket that does not exist (booking 99999)\n  BEGIN\n    cancel_booking(99999, v_refund);\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - a missing booking should have been stopped');\n  EXCEPTION\n    WHEN OTHERS THEN\n      DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Ticket does not exist : The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\n  END;\nEND;\n/\nROLLBACK;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Constraints\nUNIQUE, CHECK, NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY and a trigger each refuse bad data."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET AUTOCOMMIT OFF\nSET SERVEROUTPUT ON\n-- 1) The same e-mail twice\nBEGIN\n  INSERT INTO passengers (first_name, last_name, email, phone, date_of_birth, gender)\n  VALUES ('Test', 'Duplicate', 'aarav.sharma@example.com', '9000000001', DATE '2000-01-01', 'M');\n  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - a duplicate e-mail should have been stopped');\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Same e-mail twice       : The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\nEND;\n/\n-- 2) A seat class that does not exist\nBEGIN\n  INSERT INTO seats (flight_id, seat_no, seat_class)\n  VALUES (2, '20A', 'LUXURY');\n  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - LUXURY should have been stopped');\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Made-up seat class      : The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\nEND;\n/\n-- 3) A passenger with no first name\nBEGIN\n  INSERT INTO passengers (first_name, last_name, email, phone, date_of_birth, gender)\n  VALUES (NULL, 'Nameless', 'nameless@example.com', '9000000002', DATE '2000-01-01', 'F');\n  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - a missing name should have been stopped');\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No first name           : The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\nEND;\n/\n-- 4) A booking for a passenger who does not exist\nBEGIN\n  INSERT INTO bookings (passenger_id, seat_id, status)\n  VALUES (9999, (SELECT seat_id FROM seats WHERE flight_id = 2 AND seat_no = '1A'), 'CONFIRMED');\n  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - a missing passenger should have been stopped');\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Passenger not found     : The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\nEND;\n/\n-- 5) A flight that lands before it takes off\nBEGIN\n  INSERT INTO flights (flight_no, airline_id, origin_airport_id, dest_airport_id,\n                       departure_time, arrival_time, base_fare)\n  VALUES ('AI-999', 1, 1, 2, SYSDATE + 10, SYSDATE + 9, 5000);\n  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - landing before take-off should have been stopped');\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Lands before take-off   : The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\nEND;\n/\n-- 6) A flight from an airport to itself\nBEGIN\n  INSERT INTO flights (flight_no, airline_id, origin_airport_id, dest_airport_id,\n                       departure_time, arrival_time, base_fare)\n  VALUES ('AI-998', 1, 1, 1, SYSDATE + 10, SYSDATE + 11, 5000);\n  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - a flight to itself should have been stopped');\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Airport to itself       : The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\nEND;\n/\nROLLBACK;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Delete rules\nNO ACTION refuses, SET NULL keeps the row, CASCADE deletes the related rows."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET AUTOCOMMIT OFF\nSET SERVEROUTPUT ON\n-- Rule 1 - protect it: an airport that flights still use...\nBEGIN\n  DELETE FROM airports WHERE airport_id = 1;\n  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - the airport should have been protected');\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Airport in use          : The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\nEND;\n/\n-- ...and a flight that already has bookings.\nBEGIN\n  DELETE FROM flights WHERE flight_id = 1;\n  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('OOPS - the flight should have been protected');\nEXCEPTION\n  WHEN OTHERS THEN\n    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Flight has bookings     : The database said NO -> ' || SUBSTR(SQLERRM, 1, INSTR(SQLERRM || CHR(10), CHR(10)) - 1));\nEND;\n/\nROLLBACK;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET AUTOCOMMIT OFF\n-- Rule 2 - keep it, forget the link: flight 12 is flown by aircraft 15.\n-- Before: the flight names its aircraft.\nSELECT flight_no, aircraft_id FROM flights WHERE flight_id = 12;\nDELETE FROM aircraft WHERE aircraft_id = 15;\n-- After: the flight is still here, but the aircraft is now empty.\nSELECT flight_no, aircraft_id FROM flights WHERE flight_id = 12;\nROLLBACK;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET AUTOCOMMIT OFF\n-- Rule 3 - delete the related things too: passenger 15 has a booking and a payment.\n-- Before:\nSELECT (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bookings WHERE passenger_id = 15) AS total_bookings,\n       (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM payments WHERE booking_id = 15)   AS total_payments,\n       (SELECT status FROM seats WHERE seat_id = 144)          AS seat_status\n  FROM dual;\n\nDELETE FROM passengers WHERE passenger_id = 15;\n\n-- After: the booking and payment are gone, the seat is free again...\nSELECT (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bookings WHERE passenger_id = 15) AS total_bookings,\n       (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM payments WHERE booking_id = 15)   AS total_payments,\n       (SELECT status FROM seats WHERE seat_id = 144)          AS seat_status\n  FROM dual;\n\n-- ...and the diary noted it.\nSELECT log_id, booking_id, action, old_status, new_status\n  FROM booking_audit_log\n WHERE action = 'DELETE';\nROLLBACK;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Queries\nFifteen queries: joins, grouping, subqueries and set operators."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 1: Which flights can I still book?   (INNER JOIN)\nSELECT f.flight_no,\n       al.airline_name,\n       ao.iata_code                                     AS origin,\n       ad.iata_code                                     AS destination,\n       TO_CHAR(f.departure_time, 'DD-Mon-YYYY HH24:MI') AS departs,\n       f.base_fare,\n       f.status                                         AS flight_status\n  FROM flights f\n  JOIN airlines al ON al.airline_id = f.airline_id\n  JOIN airports ao ON ao.airport_id = f.origin_airport_id\n  JOIN airports ad ON ad.airport_id = f.dest_airport_id\n WHERE f.status IN ('SCHEDULED', 'DELAYED')\n ORDER BY f.departure_time;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 2: Who booked which seat, and how much did they pay?   (INNER JOIN of five tables)\nSELECT b.booking_id,\n       p.first_name || ' ' || p.last_name AS passenger_name,\n       f.flight_no,\n       s.seat_no,\n       s.seat_class,\n       pay.amount,\n       pay.payment_method\n  FROM bookings   b\n  JOIN passengers p   ON p.passenger_id = b.passenger_id\n  JOIN seats      s   ON s.seat_id      = b.seat_id\n  JOIN flights    f   ON f.flight_id    = s.flight_id\n  JOIN payments   pay ON pay.booking_id = b.booking_id\n WHERE b.status = 'CONFIRMED'\n ORDER BY b.booking_id;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 3: How many flights does each airline have? Airlines with none still count as 0.\n-- (LEFT OUTER JOIN)  Look for Lufthansa at the bottom.\nSELECT al.airline_name,\n       COUNT(f.flight_id) AS flights_operated\n  FROM airlines al\n  LEFT OUTER JOIN flights f ON f.airline_id = al.airline_id\n GROUP BY al.airline_name\n ORDER BY flights_operated DESC, al.airline_name;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 4: Which aircraft have no flight at the moment?   (RIGHT OUTER JOIN)\nSELECT ac.registration_no,\n       ac.aircraft_model,\n       ac.status AS aircraft_status\n  FROM flights f\n RIGHT OUTER JOIN aircraft ac ON ac.aircraft_id = f.aircraft_id\n WHERE f.flight_id IS NULL\n ORDER BY ac.registration_no;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 5: Who works on which flight? People with no flight yet say 'not rostered'.\n-- (FULL OUTER JOIN)\nSELECT c.full_name,\n       c.crew_role,\n       NVL(TO_CHAR(fc.flight_id), 'not rostered') AS rostered_flight\n  FROM crew c\n  FULL OUTER JOIN flight_crew fc ON fc.crew_id = c.crew_id\n ORDER BY fc.flight_id, c.crew_id;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 6: How much money came in for each way of paying?   (GROUP BY and totals)\nSELECT payment_method,\n       COUNT(*)                          AS payments_made,\n       SUM(amount)                       AS gross_amount,\n       SUM(refund_amount)                AS refunded_amount,\n       SUM(amount) - SUM(refund_amount)  AS net_amount\n  FROM payments\n GROUP BY payment_method\n ORDER BY net_amount DESC;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 7: Which cities have at least 2 confirmed bookings?   (GROUP BY ... HAVING)\nSELECT ad.city AS destination_city,\n       COUNT(*) AS confirmed_bookings\n  FROM bookings b\n  JOIN seats    s  ON s.seat_id     = b.seat_id\n  JOIN flights  f  ON f.flight_id   = s.flight_id\n  JOIN airports ad ON ad.airport_id = f.dest_airport_id\n WHERE b.status = 'CONFIRMED'\n GROUP BY ad.city\nHAVING COUNT(*) >= 2\n ORDER BY confirmed_bookings DESC, ad.city;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 8: Which flights cost more than the average flight?   (a question inside a question)\nSELECT flight_no, base_fare\n  FROM flights\n WHERE base_fare > (SELECT AVG(base_fare) FROM flights)\n ORDER BY base_fare DESC;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 9: Who is sitting in Business or First class?   (subquery with IN)\nSELECT p.passenger_id,\n       p.first_name || ' ' || p.last_name AS passenger_name,\n       p.email\n  FROM passengers p\n WHERE p.passenger_id IN (SELECT b.passenger_id\n                            FROM bookings b\n                            JOIN seats s ON s.seat_id = b.seat_id\n                           WHERE b.status = 'CONFIRMED'\n                             AND s.seat_class IN ('BUSINESS', 'FIRST'))\n ORDER BY p.passenger_id;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 10: Which flights cost more than the average of THEIR OWN airline?\n-- (correlated subquery: the inner question is asked again for every flight)\nSELECT f.flight_no,\n       al.airline_name,\n       f.base_fare\n  FROM flights f\n  JOIN airlines al ON al.airline_id = f.airline_id\n WHERE f.base_fare > (SELECT AVG(f2.base_fare)\n                        FROM flights f2\n                       WHERE f2.airline_id = f.airline_id)\n ORDER BY al.airline_name, f.base_fare DESC;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 11: Who has cancelled a booking at least once?   (EXISTS)\nSELECT p.passenger_id,\n       p.first_name || ' ' || p.last_name AS passenger_name\n  FROM passengers p\n WHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1\n                 FROM bookings b\n                WHERE b.passenger_id = p.passenger_id\n                  AND b.status = 'CANCELLED')\n ORDER BY p.passenger_id;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 12: Which upcoming flights have no crew yet?   (NOT EXISTS)\nSELECT f.flight_no,\n       ao.iata_code                                     AS origin,\n       ad.iata_code                                     AS destination,\n       TO_CHAR(f.departure_time, 'DD-Mon-YYYY HH24:MI') AS departs\n  FROM flights f\n  JOIN airports ao ON ao.airport_id = f.origin_airport_id\n  JOIN airports ad ON ad.airport_id = f.dest_airport_id\n WHERE f.status IN ('SCHEDULED', 'DELAYED')\n   AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1\n                     FROM flight_crew fc\n                    WHERE fc.flight_id = f.flight_id)\n ORDER BY f.departure_time;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 13: Every city we fly from OR to, each listed once.   (UNION)\nSELECT ao.city AS city\n  FROM flights f\n  JOIN airports ao ON ao.airport_id = f.origin_airport_id\nUNION\nSELECT ad.city\n  FROM flights f\n  JOIN airports ad ON ad.airport_id = f.dest_airport_id\n ORDER BY city;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 14: Which airports are BOTH a place planes leave from AND arrive at?   (INTERSECT)\nSELECT a.iata_code AS airport_code, a.city\n  FROM airports a\n  JOIN flights f ON f.origin_airport_id = a.airport_id\nINTERSECT\nSELECT a.iata_code, a.city\n  FROM airports a\n  JOIN flights f ON f.dest_airport_id = a.airport_id\n ORDER BY 1;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Question 15: Which airports are only ever a place planes ARRIVE at?   (MINUS)\nSELECT a.iata_code AS airport_code, a.city\n  FROM airports a\n  JOIN flights f ON f.dest_airport_id = a.airport_id\nMINUS\nSELECT a.iata_code, a.city\n  FROM airports a\n  JOIN flights f ON f.origin_airport_id = a.airport_id\n ORDER BY 1;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Full map\nEvery table with its columns. The line colour shows the delete rule.\n\n![Full map](airline_erd_detail.png)"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Tables\nRow counts, then every column."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Rows in each table\nSELECT 'airlines' AS table_name, COUNT(*) AS row_count FROM airlines\nUNION ALL SELECT 'airports',          COUNT(*) FROM airports\nUNION ALL SELECT 'aircraft',          COUNT(*) FROM aircraft\nUNION ALL SELECT 'flights',           COUNT(*) FROM flights\nUNION ALL SELECT 'passengers',        COUNT(*) FROM passengers\nUNION ALL SELECT 'seats',             COUNT(*) FROM seats\nUNION ALL SELECT 'bookings',          COUNT(*) FROM bookings\nUNION ALL SELECT 'payments',          COUNT(*) FROM payments\nUNION ALL SELECT 'crew',              COUNT(*) FROM crew\nUNION ALL SELECT 'flight_crew',       COUNT(*) FROM flight_crew\nUNION ALL SELECT 'booking_audit_log', COUNT(*) FROM booking_audit_log;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Every table and every column: its type, whether it is required, and what kind of key it is\nSELECT c.table_name,\n       c.column_id                                                           AS pos,\n       c.column_name,\n       CASE\n         WHEN c.data_type IN ('VARCHAR2', 'CHAR') THEN c.data_type || '(' || c.char_length || ')'\n         WHEN c.data_type = 'NUMBER' AND c.data_precision IS NOT NULL\n           THEN 'NUMBER(' || c.data_precision || CASE WHEN c.data_scale > 0 THEN ',' || c.data_scale END || ')'\n         ELSE c.data_type\n       END                                                                   AS data_type,\n       DECODE(c.nullable, 'N', 'required', 'optional')                       AS filled_in,\n       (SELECT LISTAGG(DECODE(k.constraint_type, 'P', 'primary key', 'R', 'foreign key', 'U', 'unique'), ', ')\n                 WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY k.constraint_type)\n          FROM user_cons_columns cc\n          JOIN user_constraints  k ON k.constraint_name = cc.constraint_name\n         WHERE cc.table_name  = c.table_name\n           AND cc.column_name = c.column_name\n           AND k.constraint_type IN ('P', 'R', 'U'))                         AS key_kind\n  FROM user_tab_columns c\n  JOIN user_tables      t ON t.table_name = c.table_name\n ORDER BY c.table_name, c.column_id;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Links between tables\nForeign keys and what happens on delete."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Every link between tables, and what happens when the thing it points to is deleted\nSELECT c.table_name      AS child_table,\n       r.table_name      AS parent_table,\n       c.delete_rule\n  FROM user_constraints c\n  JOIN user_constraints r ON r.constraint_name = c.r_constraint_name\n WHERE c.constraint_type = 'R'\n ORDER BY c.delete_rule, c.table_name, r.table_name;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Views\n`available_seats`, `passenger_itinerary`, `airline_revenue`."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- View available_seats: the seats still free on flight AI-101 (exactly one: 1B)\nSELECT flight_no, origin, destination, seat_no, seat_class, base_fare\n  FROM available_seats\n WHERE flight_id = 1;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- View passenger_itinerary: passenger 1's tickets (one CONFIRMED, one CANCELLED)\nSELECT booking_id, passenger_name, flight_no, seat_no, booking_status, amount_paid\n  FROM passenger_itinerary\n WHERE passenger_id = 1;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- View airline_revenue: money earned by each airline (Lufthansa has no flights and shows zero)\nSELECT airline_name, total_bookings, confirmed_bookings,\n       gross_revenue, total_refunds, net_revenue\n  FROM airline_revenue\n ORDER BY net_revenue DESC, airline_name;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Functions\n`calculate_fare` and `seats_left`."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Flight 2: 4 seats left, business costs 10,500 (4,200 x 2.5)\n-- Flight 1: nearly full, so business costs 15 percent extra: 5,800 x 2.5 x 1.15 = 16,675\n-- Flight 13: leaves within 2 days, so economy costs 20 percent extra\nSELECT seats_left(2)                 AS seats_left_flight_2,\n       calculate_fare(2, 'BUSINESS') AS business_fare_flight_2,\n       calculate_fare(1, 'BUSINESS') AS business_fare_busy_flight_1,\n       calculate_fare(13, 'ECONOMY') AS economy_fare_last_minute_flight_13\n  FROM dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Procedures\n`book_ticket`, `cancel_booking`, `show_passenger_bookings`."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- Every function, procedure, package and trigger in the system, and whether it is healthy (VALID)\nSELECT object_type, object_name, status\n  FROM user_objects\n WHERE object_type IN ('FUNCTION', 'PROCEDURE', 'PACKAGE', 'PACKAGE BODY', 'TRIGGER')\n ORDER BY object_type, object_name;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "SET SERVEROUTPUT ON\n-- show_passenger_bookings reads a passenger's tickets one at a time (an explicit cursor)\n-- and prints them, then adds up what the passenger really spent after refunds.\nBEGIN\n  show_passenger_bookings(1);\nEND;\n/"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Package\n`reservation_pkg` bundles the same functions and procedures."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- The same answers, through the package\nSELECT reservation_pkg.seats_left(2)                 AS seats_left,\n       reservation_pkg.calculate_fare(2, 'BUSINESS') AS business_fare\n  FROM dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Triggers\nFive triggers, one of them a compound trigger."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- The five triggers (all VALID). One is COMPOUND.\nSELECT trigger_name, trigger_type, triggering_event, table_name, status\n  FROM user_triggers\n ORDER BY table_name, trigger_name;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Final check\nBack to the original 18 bookings and 18 payments."
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "-- The data is exactly as it was before the demo\nSELECT (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bookings) AS total_bookings,\n       (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM payments) AS total_payments\n  FROM dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
